SF0156SS001/ADOPTED
Page 5-after line 21 Insert:
"Section 2. Nothing in this act shall prevent a school district from
expending funds generated by the foundation program that are transferred to a
special reserve fund to complete a project that is in progress. A project shall
be deemed "in progress" only if expenditures for planning, design or any phase
of construction were made prior to the effective date of this act. The school
district shall report foundation program amounts expended on a project pursuant
to this section to the state superintendent of public instruction and the state
construction department not later than July 1 of each fiscal year in which these
funds are expended. The Wyoming department of education and the state
construction department shall report to the joint education interim committee,
the select committee on school facilities and the joint appropriations committee
not later than September 1 of each year in which a report on these funds is
provided to the state superintendent of public instruction and the state
construction department.".
Page 6-line 1 Delete "Section 2." and insert "Section 3.". SCHULER,
CHAIRMAN
